J ♠Q ♠K ♦A`.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The hand contains a Rocket (Black Joker + Red Joker), a small Bomb (3333), several pairs (55, 66, 99), and a single 2. There is a potential long straight from 8 to A (7 cards) which utilizes the single 8, 10, J, Q, K, A and one 9 from the triplet. Playing this straight is the strongest opening move because an Ace-high straight cannot be beaten by any other straight (as 2s are not used in straights), forcing opponents to use a bomb or pass. This play clears 7 cards instantly and keeps the initiative. The remaining hand is very structured: the 3333 bomb can be used as a "Four with two pairs" (3333 + 55 + 66) to clear 8 more cards, leaving just a pair of 9s, a 2, and the Rocket to finish.\n\nReason: The straight `♦8 ♦9 ♣10 ♣J ♠Q ♠K ♦A` is the longest and highest possible straight available, guaranteed to win the round unless an opponent uses a bomb. It effectively clears isolated single cards and sets up a follow-up play with the `3333` combined with pairs `55` and `66` (Four-with-two-pairs), leading to a quick and secure victory.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦8", "♦9", "♣10", "♣J", "♠Q", "♠K", "♦A"]}'}
