he multiplier. Now, it\'s highly unlikely they *don\'t* beat that pair.\n\nSo, the optimal move is to play the Pair of 9s first. It maximizes the scoring potential while retaining the guaranteed win from the Rocket.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold a Rocket (Black Joker + Red Joker) and a Pair of 9s (♠9 ♣9). The Rocket is the highest possible combination and can beat anything. Since you only have these two sets of cards (2 moves to empty hand), and you have the initiative (Free Play), you are guaranteed to win regardless of which you play first. Breaking the pair of 9s into singles would be a mistake as it would require 3 turns to finish, giving opponents a chance to intercept.\n\nReason: Playing the Pair of 9s first is the best move to maximize the game score while maintaining a 100% win rate. By leading with the pair, you invite opponents to play cards—potentially a Bomb (e.g., the four missing 4s)—which would double the score multiplier. You can then beat any response with the Rocket to win the game. Playing the Rocket first also guarantees a win but denies opponents the chance to bomb, potentially resulting in a lower score.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠9", "♣9"]}'}
